<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44198" root="&#xA;                        نام&#xA;                    " body-key="n1">
                        
                            1
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَامَتْ رِجْلُهُ</span></b> 
                         (assumed tropical:)  <i>I. q.</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَدِرَتْ</span> [<i>His leg,</i> or <i>foot,
became benumbed,</i> or <i>torpid</i>]. (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بسر</span>.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَامَ</span> (assumed tropical:)  <i>It</i> (a woman's anklet) <i>ceased to sound,</i>
by reason of the fulness of the leg: like as one
says [in the contr. case], <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">استيقظ</span>. (TA in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يقظ</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَامَ</span> has for its inf. ns. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَوْمٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنَامٌ</span>.
(Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَامَ الثَّوْبُ</span>
                        <i>i. q.</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَقَدَ</span> [q. v.] (A, art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رقد</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَامَتِ السُّوقُ</span>
                        <i>i. q.</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَقَدَت</span> [q. v.] (Th, in
TA, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رقد</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b6-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَامَ</span> (tropical:)  <i>He lay; as opposed to
he sat and he stood.</i> See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَائِمٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b7-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَامَ عَنْ حَاجَتِهِ</span>
                        <i>He cared not for the object of his want, neglected
it.</i> (Msb.)

